            <ArticleTitle>Retrograde approach &quot;reverse CART technique&quot; with a single guiding catheter for chronic total occlusion of the right coronary artery via an anomalous left circumflex artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E92-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The retrograde approach has been shown to improve the success rate of percutaneous coronary intervention for coronary chronic total occlusion (CTO) when performed by highly experienced operators. We report a very challenging case of a retrograde approach by the &quot;reverse controlled antegrade and retrograde subintimal tracking (CART) technique&quot; with a single guiding catheter for a CTO of the right coronary artery via an anomalous left circumflex artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
